body:
Library agent-guide layout: the library layout ignores every top-level entry that is not part of the library structure (`library.yaml`, `slides/`, `sections/`, `themes/`, `media/`), including `AGENTS.md` (the library/template-author agent guide, library-agent-guide). A library root may hold `AGENTS.md` alongside `library.yaml`, `slides/`, `sections/`, `themes/` and `media/`; it is inert — never parsed as YAML/template, validated, rendered, listed or served — and is NOT a template asset. The loader ignores every top-level entry that is not part of the library structure (templates-dir-layout): it validates only the library itself, so the guide is permitted with no special case, and a library that is a git repo (`.git/`) or carries a README or other unrelated files also loads. The rule is specific to the library (templates) root; the deck root has no top-level-entry rule and its `AGENTS.md` is unaffected.

AC:
- `kalide init-library ../lib` writes `../lib/AGENTS.md` and `../lib` still loads cleanly (templates-dir-validation);
- a library root holding an unrelated top-level entry (e.g. `.git/`, `README.md`, `notes.txt`) still loads cleanly and that entry is ignored;
- `../lib/AGENTS.md` is ignored by load/validate/render/serve/list (the guide is not a template asset).
